From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 19:17:22 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] media: venus: hfi_cmds: packetize the H.264 8x8 transform for
 HFI 3xx

venc sets HFI_PROPERTY_PARAM_VENC_H264_TRANSFORM_8X8 for every H.264
session, but only the 4xx packetizer knows the property. On 3xx firmware
(MSM8998) the set falls through to the 1x packetizer, which rejects it,
so session configuration fails and REQBUFS returns -EINVAL: no H.264
encode works at all on these SoCs, while HEVC and VP8 do.

The 3xx firmware accepts the property: the downstream msm8998 vidc driver
sends the same id (VENC_COMMON_START + 0x025) as a single u32 enable, which
is exactly struct hfi_h264_8x8_transform. Handle it in the 3xx packetizer.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
---
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/hfi_cmds.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/hfi_cmds.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/hfi_cmds.c
index 3ae063094e3e..9684ecb5f47d 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/hfi_cmds.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/hfi_cmds.c
@@ -1177,6 +1177,13 @@ pkt_session_set_property_3xx(struct hfi_session_set_property_pkt *pkt,
 	case HFI_PROPERTY_PARAM_VDEC_CONTINUE_DATA_TRANSFER:
 		/* for 3xx fw version session_continue is used */
 		break;
+	case HFI_PROPERTY_PARAM_VENC_H264_TRANSFORM_8X8: {
+		struct hfi_h264_8x8_transform *in = pdata, *tm = prop_data;
+
+		tm->enable_type = in->enable_type;
+		pkt->shdr.hdr.size += sizeof(u32) + sizeof(*tm);
+		break;
+	}
 	default:
 		ret = pkt_session_set_property_1x(pkt, cookie, ptype, pdata);
 		break;
